{"kind":"request","text":"G2: measurements from the chat (plan 033, notes/plans/033-2026-10-18-grow-room-demo.md on main, order step 5; grow note notes/2026-10-17-grow-operation-application-design.md, section 4 \"Morning\", section 6.1 items and acts, section 6.2 view description, section 7 G2). Needs G1, landed at main b54f8880. Start now; G2 and G3 stay ahead of P1 to P3.\n\nScope. Three things, on G1's declarations and the kit, with no view code in the host.\n1. The tender's probe through the model. A tender types numbers and words into the chat (\"bench C4, moisture 31, EC 2.1, pH 5.9\"); the model makes the one `probe` act of G0's room definition for her through the tool the view description derives; the host validates the arguments and signs the act with her key under `grow.tend`. Decision: a declared act may carry declared parameters (name, kind, unit, range or allowed words) beside G1's constant arguments; the derived tool exposes them as its input schema and the model fills them from the typed text. Probes are text (plan 033, decision 2): moisture, conductivity, acidity, height and a scouting note; no photo, no custody.\n2. The bench carousel: a `carousel` view over the `bench` item ordered by oldest last probe, showing the last values and their age and the hint to type the new probe in the chat (mockup tender-bench); after the probe is accepted the card advances to the next bench. At most two acts per card, as G1 decided.\n3. The three grid layers on the grid surface: temperature from the sensors' readings, moisture from probes, scouting from the scouting notes. Each layer shades a cell by value and by the age of its reading, so a bench nobody has probed for two days is visible; the layer switch is in the surface; a cell opens the declared zone or bench view. The layer data is a declared projection the generic interface serves (M2a), not host code.\n\nDone when a probe typed in a chat appears in its layer and advances the carousel, inside the kit's test host with the kit's checks, each named in the review request with its witness: (a) the typed text becomes one signed `probe` act with its values, through the derived tool, and the bench's revision advances; (b) the carousel shows the next oldest bench; (c) the moisture layer cell for that bench shows the new value with age zero, and the stale bench reads as stale before it; (d) a probe for a bench at a stale revision, or by a member without `grow.tend`, is refused by the guard and shown as the kit's stale refusal; (e) app-only data, quiet context (the model receives the context line, never the card's data), receipts, resize. Gate passed once; measurements labelled by how they were taken; checker approval at the exact head. One head, or two if the layers split from the probe and carousel; say which.\n\nOut of scope: routing of tasks and requests (G3), the native device-command record (G5a), the hosted room and the /grow/ page (G5), rendering in the browser page (G6), photos and custody, real sensors. Open points go to planner as asserts; the parameter decision above is final unless the form cannot carry it, in which case say what it needs.","body":{"conditions":"a probe typed in a chat appears in its layer and advances the carousel, inside the kit's test host with the kit's checks named with their witnesses; gate passed once; checker approval at the exact head","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}